{
  "capitulo": 5,
  "titulo_es": "Cuando era niño",
  "titulo": { "en": "When I was a child" },
  "intro": { "en": "The imperfect describes how things used to be, with no clear end." },
  "palabras": {
    "era": { "en": "I was, he/she was (used to be)", "pron": "E-ra", "cat": "verb" },
    "tenía": { "en": "I had, he/she had", "pron": "te-NI-a", "cat": "verb" },
    "vivía": { "en": "I lived, he/she lived", "pron": "bi-BI-a", "cat": "verb" },
    "iba": { "en": "I used to go, he/she used to go", "pron": "I-ba", "cat": "verb" },
    "cuando": { "en": "when", "pron": "KWAN-do", "cat": "conjunction" },
    "niño": { "en": "child, boy", "pron": "NI-nyo", "genero": "m" },
    "antes": { "en": "before, in the past", "pron": "AN-tes", "cat": "adverb" },
    "siempre": { "en": "always", "pron": "SYEM-pre", "cat": "adverb" }
  },
  "bloques": [
    {
      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": "Background, not a single event",
      "texto": "The **imperfecto** is for habits and descriptions in the past.\n\n- Cuando **era** niño, **vivía** en Lima.\n- **Tenía** un perro.\n- Siempre **iba** al parque.\n\n**-ar** verbs use **-aba**. **-er** and **-ir** verbs use **-ía**. Ser is **era**. Ir is **iba**. For **tú**, add **-s**: tenías, ibas."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tabla",
      "titulo": "Three useful forms",
      "columnas": ["yo / él", "imperfecto"],
      "filas": [
        ["ser", "era"],
        ["tener", "tenía"],
        ["ir", "iba"],
        ["vivir", "vivía"]
      ],
      "nota": "Yo and él/ella share the same form: yo era, él era."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "dialogo",
      "titulo": "Childhood",
      "frases": [
        {
          "quien": "Pablo",
          "es": "Cuando era niño, vivía en Lima.",
          "en": "When I was a child, I lived in Lima.",
          "analisis": [
            ["Cuando", "when"],
            ["era niño", "I was a child"],
            ["vivía", "I lived"],
            ["en Lima", "place"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Lucía",
          "es": "¿Tenías hermanos?",
          "en": "Did you have brothers or sisters?",
          "analisis": [
            ["¿Tenías", "did you have"],
            ["hermanos", "siblings"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Pablo",
          "es": "Sí, tenía una hermana.",
          "en": "Yes, I had a sister.",
          "analisis": [
            ["tenía", "I had"],
            ["una hermana", "a sister"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Lucía",
          "es": "Antes yo siempre iba al parque.",
          "en": "I always used to go to the park.",
          "analisis": [
            ["Antes", "in the past"],
            ["siempre", "always"],
            ["iba", "I used to go"],
            ["al parque", "to the park"]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "vocabulario",
      "palabras": ["era", "tenía", "vivía", "iba", "cuando", "niño", "antes", "siempre"]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "huecos",
      "id": "a2-imp-era",
      "pregunta": { "en": "Complete: when I was a child." },
      "frase": "Cuando ___ niño, vivía en Lima.",
      "audio": true,
      "opciones": {
        "era": { "en": "A description in the past uses the imperfect: era." },
        "fui": { "en": "Fui is one finished moment, not a whole childhood." },
        "soy": { "en": "Soy is the present." }
      },
      "correcta": "era"
    },
    {
      "tipo": "ordenar",
      "id": "a2-imp-parque",
      "frase": "Siempre iba al parque",
      "traduccion": { "en": "I always used to go to the park." }
    }
  ]
}
